# Files Cloudflare must NOT publish.
#
# The whole working directory is uploaded as static assets, so anything not
# listed here is reachable on the public site. That is not a theoretical risk:
# .git was being served, which let anyone reconstruct the entire repository and
# its full history, including every file ever deleted from it.
#
# It also broke the build. The pack file grew past Cloudflare's 25 MiB limit for
# a single asset, so the deploy started failing outright - the exposure and the
# broken build were the same bug.

# version control - never publish
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# project files, not content
tools
articulos
serve.py
wrangler.toml
README.md
.atl
.claude

# editor and OS leftovers
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
